{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": "`sched.next_run(now, hour, minute, tz)` should return the next wall-clock time at\n`hour:minute` in timezone `tz` that is strictly after `now`, as an aware datetime in that\nzone. Users in Europe/Berlin report it skips a day after 22:00 UTC, and that around the\nDST change in March it returns a time that is off by one hour. `tests/test_sched.py`\nreproduces the first bug. Find the root cause of both, fix the function, keep the\nsignature. Run the tests."}, "timestamp": "2026-10-09T16:26:19.308Z"}
