{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfryc44bxPMZnJ8iSWRv3","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both bugs are fixed in `sched/core.py` and `tests/test_sched.py` passes (2 tests). The signature is unchanged. I did not commit.\n\n**Root causes**\n\n1. **Skipped day after 22:00 UTC:** `today = now.date()` takes the calendar date in UTC, not in `tz`. Between 22:00 and 24:00 UTC, Berlin is already on the next day, so the function computed the wrong \"today\". In the test case it returned `2026-06-02 01:00 Berlin`, which is before `now`, so the result was not after `now`.\n2. **One-hour error around DST:** the fallback added `timedelta(days=1)` to the instant in UTC. A local day is 23 or 25 hours on a DST change day, so the wall-clock time drifted. My probe showed a 09:00 job on March 28 returning 10:00 on March 29.\n\n**Fix**\n\n- `today = now.astimezone(zone).date()` takes the date in the target zone.\n- When today's time has passed, the function now steps the calendar date (`today + 1 day`) and builds the wall-clock time in `zone`. It no longer shifts the instant by 24h.\n\n**Test changes**\n\n- I added `test_next_day_keeps_wall_clock_across_dst_change` to cover the DST bug. The existing test already covered the first bug. The new test is my addition, so drop it if you only wanted the existing test run.\n\n**Side effects**\n\n- Running pytest rewrote the tracked `.pyc` files under `__pycache__`. I restored them with `git checkout`, so the working tree only has the two source files changed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2459,"cache_read_input_tokens":55618,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2459},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":n